dist/
build/
.next/
out/
bin/
*.exe

# Environment files
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
# M10-4 #72: goreleaser before.hooks copies .env.example -> default.env.example
# at release time so the GitHub asset name and SHA256SUMS entry stay aligned
# (GitHub release assets cannot start with a dot). The copy is build-only.
default.env.example

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Test coverage
coverage/
coverage.out
coverage.html
*.test

# Playwright test results
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Temporary files
tmp/
temp/

# Misc
*.pem
.turbo

# Enterprise self-host (M4-6): actual secrets and backups must never be committed.
# Only the *.sample files under docker/secrets.example/ are tracked.
/docker/secrets/
/docker/backups/

# GoReleaser output (M5-2 / #54): llm-bench release archives + checksums.
# CI uploads these to the GitHub Release; nothing in /dist/ belongs in git.
/dist/

# Standalone lint tools under tools/ — `go build ./...` inside a module
# drops a binary named after the module directory next to its main.go.
# CI always invokes them with `go run .`, so the binary is never wanted in
# git; left unignored, a `git add -A` after a local build sweeps a ~4 MB
# host-arch executable into the commit (the same class of accident as the
# node_modules commit that once produced 421K insertions).
#
# Measured before this entry existed: `go build ./...` in each module left
#   ?? tools/lint-migration-locks/lint-migration-locks
#   ?? tools/lint-migration-rls/lint-migration-rls
# untracked and unignored. tools/lint-toolchain-alignment already carries
# its own module-local .gitignore for the same reason, which is why it did
# not show up.
#
# Listed explicitly, one line per module, rather than as a `/tools/*/lint-*`
# wildcard: that wildcard would also swallow a future tracked source file
# whose name happens to start with `lint-`. When a new tool lands under
# tools/, add its line here — .github/workflows/repo-hygiene.yml fails the
# build if a tools module's `go build` leaves the worktree dirty, so the
# omission is caught at PR time rather than in a stray commit.
/tools/lint-ci-inventory/lint-ci-inventory
/tools/lint-migration-locks/lint-migration-locks
/tools/lint-migration-rls/lint-migration-rls
